<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigurd Eysteinsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 892</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Sigurd the Mighty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigurd Eysteinsson, called the Mighty, was according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkneyinga-saga">Orkneyinga saga</a> the first Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a>, in the late 9th century. Brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rognvald-eysteinsson">Rognvald Eysteinsson</a>, Earl of Møre, he received the islands from him after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> granted them to Rognvald. Sigurd extended Norse power into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and, according to the sagas, died from a wound caused by the tooth of a slain enemy, Máel Brigte.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sigurd-eysteinsson.jpg" alt="Sigurd Eysteinsson" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:DrKay · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sigurd_Eysteinsson%27s_Scotland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
